            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Entity manager by definition should not have references to device tree, so this is arguably correct."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for your review @ed@tanous.net!\n\nI was unsure if the GPIO Pin Name should be defined via a meson option or via entity-manager as there are other entities like the leak detector that also use the GPIO Pin Name from the device tree (which comes from entity-manager) [1][2].\n\nSo far, it seems that no other sensor defines something similar via meson options, wouldn't this add inconsistency across the sensor apps?\n\n[1] https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/0c324888374388f6c268293eb65fcbe017183de8/schemas/leak_detector.json#L21\n[2] https://github.com/openbmc/dbus-sensors/blob/master/src/leakdetector/LeakDetectionManager.cpp#L136"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "These should come through meson options."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for this level of thought and care in your patch."
                }
            ],
